@node Agent Commands
@section Agent Commands
@cindex agent commands

Agent commands are bound under the @kbd{a} prefix in list, show, and
dashboard buffers, and the full menu is on @kbd{a} in the dispatch menu
(@pxref{Transients}).

@table @kbd
@kindex s
@item s
Start an agent on the issue at point.  This opens the launch transient
described below.
@kindex w
@item w
Sling the issue to a worktree.
@kindex S
@item S
Stop the agent session at point.
@kindex j
@item j
Jump to the agent buffer.
@kindex p
@item p
Send a prompt to the agent.
@kindex l
@item l
List active sessions.
@kindex c
@item c
Clean up stale sessions.
@kindex B
@item B
Set the default backend.
@kindex g
@item g
Refresh the session state.
@end table

The launch transient (@kbd{s}) chooses the role, target, backend, and
prompt before it launches:

@table @kbd
@kindex t
@kindex r
@item @kbd{t} @kbd{r} @kbd{p}
Role: Task (the default), Review (with a QA mode toggle), or Plan
(@kbd{p}).
@kindex T
@item @kbd{w} @kbd{T}
Target: a derived new worktree (@kbd{w}), or an existing worktree to
choose (@kbd{T}).
@kindex b
@item b
Backend, with the documented backends first and the rest in a collapsed
group.
@kindex e
@kindex P
@item @kbd{e} @kbd{P}
Edit (@kbd{e}) or preview (@kbd{P}) the user prompt.
@kindex x
@kindex q
@item @kbd{x} @kbd{q}
@kbd{s} starts the agent with the selected role, target, backend, and
prompt; @kbd{x} resets the launch parameters and @kbd{q} quits without
starting.
@end table

There is no separate @samp{Editor} role: a custom prompt is the Task role
with an edited prompt.  The type names used by the prompt protocol are still
Task, Review, Plan, QA, and Custom (@pxref{Agent Types}).

